# Galaxy on Fire 1.1.5 (www.fishlabs.net.GalaxyOnFire); installed as
# /root/n72hle-test/GalaxyOnFire.env, read by /usr/bin/n72-touchhle.
#
# Its menus draw a full-screen pattern of about 500 quads, one draw each, on
# top of a lit 3D scene: about 100 000 words of TA stream a frame when all of
# it goes through the hardware T&L, and a scene holds 65 536. With n72-gles's
# default (never split a scene for T&L draws) the meshes fell back to the CPU
# path. Split scenes instead: main menu 9 -> 19 FPS, mode screens 7 -> 14 FPS;
# the flight itself fits one scene and stays at its 30 FPS either way
# (2026-11-22, kernel #70, same seed).
export N72_GLES_VGP_SPLIT=1
